 61GA c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2017Ku12:                          
 61GA2c  Eur Phys J A53, 134 (2017)                                             
 61GA c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster), June 30, 2017                         
 61GA c  2017Ku12: {+61}Ga isotope produced in the fragmentation of             
 61GA2c  79 MeV/nucleon {+64}Zn{+29+} beam with Ni target of 236 mg/cm{+2}      
 61GA3c  thickness. Fragments were selected with the LISE3 separator at         
 61GA4c  GANIL and identified by time-of-flight and energy loss using silicon   
 61GA5c  |DE detector and implanted into a double-sided silicon strip           
 61GA6c  detector (DSSSD). The implanted ions and charged-particle decays       
 61GA7c  were detected by the DSSSD, which was surrounded by four HPGe Clover   
 61GA8c  detectors (three EXOGAM clovers and a smaller Euroball clover)         
 61GA9c  for |g-ray detection. Half-life of {+61}Ga decay was measured by       
 61GAAc  ({+61}Ga implants)|b time-correlated decay events                      
